// para.p2p (p2p P3.3) — `p2p.identity()` is this node's stable identity (the hex Ed25519 public key
// it signs with, persisted across restarts on a real host). The deterministic sandbox has no
// network identity, so it returns `none` — a program that reads it stays oracle-safe (both backends
// agree, no real key to leak into the output).
// expect: stdout "identity none"
// expect: exit 0
use para.{p2p}

id = match p2p.identity() {
    some(k) => k,
    none => "none",
}
echo "identity ${id}"
